syntax:
Use labels as subroutines and goto statements to simulate GOSUB/RETURN behavior:

label:
    // code
    if (condition) goto label;
    // continue

To emulate GOSUB, jump to a label; to emulate RETURN, jump back to a saved point or use a stack to manage return addresses.

code_example:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int state = 0;
    int return_point = 0;
    goto start;

subroutine: // Emulating GOSUB
    printf("In subroutine, state = %d\n", state);
    // Save return point
    return_point = 1; // For illustration, using a variable
    goto return_point_label;

start:
    printf("Start, state = %d\n", state);
    if (state == 0) {
        state = 1;
        goto subroutine; // GOSUB
    }
    if (return_point) {
        // Emulating RETURN
        goto after_subroutine;
    }
after_subroutine:
    printf("After subroutine, state = %d\n", state);
    return 0;
}
